<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthew Baillie Begbie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819–1894</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthew Baillie Begbie was an English-born lawyer who became the first judge of the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a> in 1858. Travelling on circuit on horseback through the goldfields, he enforced British law among the miners and earned a reputation for firmness. He was chief justice of British Columbia from 1870 until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matthew-baillie-begbie.jpg" alt="Matthew Baillie Begbie" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matthew_Baillie_Begbie.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
